L0@P0: 412.591 DUTIES OF CLERK AND TREASURER; MAY BE COMBINED.
L1@P0: Subdivision 1. Clerk not on council; transition. The clerk shall perform all the duties imposed on the
L2@P0: clerk in cities generally but shall not be a member of the council, except that when Optional Plan A is first
L3@P0: adopted in any city, the incumbent clerk shall continue to be a member of the council until the expiration
L4@P0: of the term.
L5@P0: Subd. 1a. If treasurer, duties unchanged. The duties of the treasurer if that office exists shall not be
L6@P0: affected by adoption of Optional Plan A.
L7@P0: Subd. 2. Combining, uncombining clerk-treasurer. Cities operating under Optional Plan A may, by
L8@P0: an ordinance effective after the expiration of the term of the incumbent treasurer at the date of adoption of
L9@P0: Optional Plan A, combine the offices of clerk and treasurer in the office of clerk-treasurer and thereafter the
L10@P0: duties of the treasurer as prescribed by this chapter shall be performed by the clerk-treasurer. The offices of
L11@P0: clerk and treasurer may be reestablished by ordinance.
L12@P0: Subd. 3. Auditstandardsif combined. (a) If the offices of clerk and treasurer are combined as provided
L13@P0: by this section, and the city's annual revenue for all governmental and enterprise funds combined is more
L14@P0: than the amount in paragraph (b), the council shall provide for an annual audit of the city's financial affairs
L15@P0: by the state auditor or a certified public accountant in accordance with minimum procedures prescribed by
L16@P0: the state auditor. If the offices of clerk and treasurer are combined and the city's annual revenue for all
L17@P0: governmental and enterprise funds combined isthe amount in paragraph (b), or less, the councilshall provide
L18@P0: for an audit of the city's financial affairs by the state auditor or a certified public accountant in accordance
L19@P0: with minimum audit procedures prescribed by the state auditor at least once every five years, which audit
L20@P0: shall be for a one-year period to be determined at random by the person conducting the audit.
L21@P0: (b) For the purposes of paragraph (a), the amount in 2025 is $1,000,000, and is adjusted annually
L22@P0: thereafter for inflation using the annual implicit price deflator for state and local expenditures as published
L23@P0: by the United States Department of Commerce.
